sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 + 5 (shared SSH identity), node.role_add and node.role_remove charts. swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-node-role-relocate-direct.yaml, docs/cli/node/role-relocate.mdx, docs/solutions/relocate-gateway-role.mdx.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-03, rules 1, 2, 4, 6, 9, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18, 21, 22 (swamp refused at admission; Metrics reuses its role workflow; the source reuses role:remove; no PHP pools or Metrics reconcile; pinned SSH argv; one end check).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:role:relocate
  %% kind: node.role_relocate
  %% Rule 23: 2026-11-03 required-only main path.
  %% Pinned Debian downloads use native SSH curl exit codes for transport-only fallback, then verify the pin before publication.
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>gets the role
  participant S as Node 7<br/>gives up the role
  CLI->>GW: node:role:relocate 12<br/>websocket
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:relocate 12 websocket`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> [--from=NODE] [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the target Node, by id or exact name, and the role: `gateway`, `websocket` or `metrics`
  %%> - the source is the current holder of the role, here Node 7
  %%> Optional flags:
  %%> - `--from=NODE` names the source Node; it adds no steps
  %%> - `--force` confirms the move; it is required without a terminal and with `--json`
  %%> - `--idempotency-key=KEY` reuses a key to retry the start
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  opt role is swamp
    GW--xCLI: 422 swamp role held<br/>node.role_relocate_swamp_held
    %%> Why:
    %%> - serve on the `swamp` Node runs every Swamp run, so a run cannot move it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway refuses before it records anything; no task, no run
    %%> Open:
    %%> - a live move of the `swamp` role is Nick's decision
  end
  Note over GW: Validate, move the role<br/>role: provisioning · task #5180
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - the role is `gateway`, `websocket` or `metrics`, and `--force` is given
  %%> - Node 7 holds the role; on a retry Node 12 holds it and `--from=7` names the same admitted move
  %%> - Node 12 and Node 7 are active Linux Nodes with recorded SSH management; Node 12 holds no role that conflicts
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - moves the `websocket` assignment to Node 12 with status provisioning; one assignment stays active the whole time
  %%> - copies role settings that Node 12 lacks, such as Reverb's `APP_KEY`; it never overwrites one
  %%> - for `gateway`: gives Node 12 an access grant to the `vpn` and `metrics` Nodes
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the role runtime for Node 12, its certificates, firewall and publications
  %%> - the role removal for Node 7, the same intent `node:role:remove` builds
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5180 recorded with the full intent; nothing has happened on a Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-relocate
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the target plan, the source removal, the addresses and SSH host keys of every Node the run reaches
  %%> Secrets:
  %%> - Reverb's `.env` and the Grafana password go to the Swamp vault as execution copies; the inputs hold only their key names
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no step reads the intent back from the Gateway; the inputs are the intent
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5180
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt role is metrics
    SW->>N: Apply the Metrics role<br/>child operation-metrics-enable
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the same workflow as `metrics:enable`, aimed at Node 12: Docker, configuration, Prometheus and Grafana, exporters, the Gateway site and private DNS
    %%> Keeps:
    %%> - the Gateway's `metrics.orbit` certificate; the move signs none
    %%> Why:
    %%> - one rule in one place: the Metrics runtime has one workflow
  end
  opt role is websocket
    SW->>N: Make the release folder<br/>install -d -o USER RELEASE
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - makes a new release folder beside the install path, owned by the role's user
    %%> How:
    %%> - every Node step is one `@swamp/ssh exec` argument list with the recorded host key of Node 12
    SW->>N: Clone the Reverb release<br/>git clone --no-checkout
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - clones the Reverb repository into the release folder, as the role's user
    SW->>N: Check out the Reverb ref<br/>git checkout --detach REF
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks out the commit this Gateway release pins
    SW->>N: Install Reverb packages<br/>composer install --no-dev
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - installs the release's PHP packages as the role's user
    SW->>N: Write the Reverb .env<br/>install -m 0600 /dev/stdin
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the server's `.env` from the vault copy on stdin; the value never enters argv or output
    SW->>N: Write the Reverb unit<br/>orbit-websocket.service
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the systemd unit from the intent
    SW->>N: Activate the release<br/>ln -sfnT RELEASE INSTALL
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - points the install path at the new release; a real folder there fails the step instead
  end
  opt role is gateway
    SW->>N: Write the DNS route<br/>wg-quick@orbit drop-in
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the drop-in that routes the private domain to Orbit VPN DNS whenever the tunnel starts
    %%> When:
    %%> - Node 12 is not a managed DNS peer; peer convergence owns that policy
  end
  opt role is websocket or gateway
    SW->>N: Reload unit catalogue<br/>systemctl daemon-reload
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - loads the new unit or drop-in
  end
  opt role is websocket
    SW->>N: Enable Reverb<br/>systemctl enable
    SW->>N: Restart Reverb<br/>systemctl restart
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts the new release; a rerun restarts it on the same release
  end
  opt role is gateway
    SW->>N: Route the private domain<br/>resolvectl, best effort
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - applies the route to the live `orbit` link now
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the move still succeeds; `follow_up` names `orbit node:role:add 12 gateway --converge`
  end
  opt role needs a certificate
    SW->>N: Publish the certificate<br/>child role-certificate-publish
    %%> When:
    %%> - `websocket` serves `reverb.orbit`; `gateway` serves `metrics.orbit` while Metrics exists
    %%> How:
    %%> - the key and CSR are made on Node 12; the child sends only the CSR to `operation:direct:certificate-sign`, the one Gateway call a step may make
  end
  opt role is websocket or gateway
    SW->>N: Open the role ports<br/>ufw argv, pinned SSH
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - adds the role's managed firewall rules, such as `orbit:websocket-https`
    SW->>N: Close retired ports<br/>ufw delete argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - closes public SSH recovery and retired role rules, as a role converge does
  end
  SW->>N: Publish the Caddy sites<br/>child operation-route-caddy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - publishes the complete Caddyfile of every publishing Node but Node 7, validates it and reloads Caddy
  %%> How:
  %%> - one `forEach` across the publishing Nodes; Node 7 is left for the removal
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no PHP pools: no relocatable role publishes one
  SW->>N: Publish the role DNS<br/>child route-dns-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - points the role's private DNS names, such as `reverb.orbit`, at Node 12 on the `vpn` Node
  %%> Order:
  %%> - Node 12 serves before anything leaves Node 7
  opt role is websocket
    SW->>N: Check Reverb<br/>curl 127.0.0.1:PORT
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - proves Reverb answers on its local port
  end
  opt private DNS moved
    SW->>SW: Let DNS answers expire<br/>child route-dns-grace
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - waits 31 seconds, so resolvers stop answering with Node 7 before it withdraws
  end
  SW->>S: Remove from the source<br/>child operation-node-role-remove
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same workflow as `node:role:remove`, with the intent it builds for Node 7, for every role
  %%> - not `metrics:disable` for `metrics`: it withdraws `metrics.orbit` and its certificate, which the moved role keeps
  %%> - withdraws the role's sites, PHP pools and DNS, stops and removes its units, files, containers, firewall rules and certificates
  %%> Keeps:
  %%> - role data, the Gateway checkout, its database, the Orbit CA and the SSH keys; Caddy and PHP-FPM keep running
  %%> Check:
  %%> - its own native end check proves the role is gone from Node 7
  Note over SW: Confirm the move<br/>native assert
  %%> What it checks:
  %%> - Reverb answered on Node 12, the role ports opened, and the source removal proved its end check
  %%> Why:
  %%> - one end check; the move only counts when both Nodes show it
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; no step reports back
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>role: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `websocket` role on Node 12 becomes active
    %%> - when a Metrics role exists, `follow_up` names `orbit node:role:add <metrics-node> metrics --converge`: Metrics rebuilds its scrape configuration in its own lifecycle
    %%> - Node 7's role settings and runtime records are forgotten
    %%> - task #5180 succeeds
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the role failed<br/>converge:STEP or remove:STEP
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the role stays assigned to Node 12, marked failed with the step's own error code
    %%> - task #5180 fails
    %%> On the Nodes:
    %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback
    %%> - a failure on Node 7 leaves the role serving from Node 12
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `orbit node:role:relocate 12 websocket --from=7 --force` after fixing the cause
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5180
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
